.TH RTOP 1 "2026" "rtop" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rtop \- real-time Linux telemetry graph and process manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rtop
[\fB\-\-demo\fR | \fB\-\-sysroot\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-read\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR]
.br
.B rtop \-\-stats
[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-interval\fR \fIDURATION\fR] [\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fIDURATION\fR] [\fB\-\-strict\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rtop
models processes, containers, sockets, devices, sensors and security events
as one connected graph. Without options it opens an interactive terminal
interface; with \fB\-\-stats\fR it prints the graph as YAML (or JSON) and exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-stats
Collect two samples separated by the interval and print the graph on stdout.
.TP
.B \-\-json
With \-\-stats, print JSON instead of YAML.
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " DURATION"
Rate measurement window (default 1s; e.g. 500ms, 2s).
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " DURATION"
Upper bound on \-\-stats collection; unanswered sources are reported as timed out (default 5s).
.TP
.B \-\-strict
With \-\-stats, exit with status 2 if any collector did not deliver.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Observe the built-in simulated machine.
.TP
.BI \-\-sysroot " DIR"
Observe a captured procfs/sysfs tree; process actions are disabled.
.TP
.B \-\-read\-only
Disable every process action.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-mouse
Do not capture the mouse.
.SH KEYS
\fB0\fR\-\fB9\fR views, \fBhjkl\fR move, \fBgg\fR/\fBG\fR first/last, \fB/\fR \fB?\fR search,
\fBF\fR filter, \fBEnter\fR inspect, \fBEsc\fR back, \fBs\fR\fIx\fR sort, \fBx\fR terminate,
\fBX\fR force kill, \fBgs\fR signal menu, \fBgp\fR/\fBgr\fR suspend/resume, \fB!\fR emergency mode,
\fB:\fR command line, \fBF1\fR help, \fBq\fR quit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on error, 2 when \-\-strict finds incomplete collection.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ps (1),
.BR top (1),
.BR ss (8)
